id: pm-xp1xsw
title: "Outcome milestone: v1.0 GA stability contract — frozen grammar, semver SDK surface, storage format policy, published scale targets"
description: "Outcome milestone defining the v1.0 stability contract for command grammar, semantic-versioned SDK APIs, storage compatibility, and reproducible performance claims."
type: Milestone
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: contract,ga,"horizon:gate",milestone,outcome,semver,stability
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:44:20.858Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T10:16:07.260Z"
deadline: "2027-12-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 3600
acceptance_criteria: "The CLI grammar is frozen against the contract table with alias-removal windows measured by usage counters, not guesswork; The public SDK surface carries semver commitments with a compatibility test suite proving them; Storage format_version policy defines forward and backward compatibility windows with an automated cross-version matrix; Published scale targets are backed by reproducible benchmark evidence, not claims"
goal: v1-ga-stability
objective: "Downstream users can depend on pm surfaces with written, testable compatibility guarantees"
value: Without a stability contract every consumer treats pm as pre-release and refuses to build durable integrations on it.
impact: Converts the ecosystem from experimental packages to dependable ones and makes deprecations governable instead of ad hoc.
outcome: "A published contract states what is frozen, what may change, and how long removed spellings survive — enforced by compatibility tests."
why_now: "Deferred deliberately: freezing before grammar consolidation and SDK completion would immortalise the surface this roadmap is trying to simplify."
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: medium
